From: Deskkin Gate 1C <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: map ESP32-S3 to the Rust Xtensa target

This bounded feasibility patch adds only the Zephyr-to-Rust target mapping
needed by Gate 1C. Remove it when the pinned zephyr-lang-rust revision (or its
approved successor) supplies an equivalent mapping upstream.
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index e36f503..49615d5 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -49,6 +49,8 @@ function(_rust_map_target)
     else()
       message(FATAL_ERROR "Rust: Unsupported riscv ISA")
     endif()
+  elseif(CONFIG_XTENSA AND CONFIG_SOC_SERIES_ESP32S3)
+    set(RUST_TARGET "xtensa-esp32s3-none-elf" PARENT_SCOPE)
   elseif(CONFIG_ARCH_POSIX AND CONFIG_64BIT AND (${CMAKE_HOST_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR} MATCHES "x86_64"))
     set(RUST_TARGET "x86_64-unknown-none" PARENT_SCOPE)
   elseif(CONFIG_ARCH_POSIX AND CONFIG_64BIT AND (${CMAKE_HOST_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR} MATCHES "aarch64"))
-- 
